From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:21:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/23] rocket: rk3576: neutral weights for padded pointwise
 input channels

The CMAC computes sum(x_s * w_s) and the hardware adds B * sum(x_s) with
B = 0x80 - wt_zp, both over every channel the CNA reads, padded ones
included. The pointwise packer stored padded input channels as 0, which
weighs B, not 0; the bias fold then only cancels it when the padded input
bytes hold in_zp - 0x80. That is true for an uploaded graph input but not
for a tensor written by a previous convolution of the same subgraph (the
DPU leaves 0 there). MobileNetV2 op 6 (56x56x24 -> 144) fed by op 5 was
off by a constant 49 on every channel, and the full model was 90 % wrong.

Store padded channels as wt_zp - 0x80 (neutral whatever the input holds)
and drop the padded-channel term from the weight sum. Single layers with
uploaded inputs give identical results.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c | 63 +++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
index 384b757..3a4303d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
@@ -565,6 +565,30 @@ rkt_fill_weights(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
       bool pw_flat = getenv("ROCKET_PW_FLAT") != NULL;
       bool pw_icgroup = getenv("ROCKET_PW_ICGROUP") != NULL;
 
+      /*
+       * THE PADDED INPUT CHANNELS GET THE NEUTRAL WEIGHT.
+       *
+       * The CMAC computes sum(x_s * w_s) with x_s = x - 0x80 and
+       * w_s = w_q - 0x80 as stored, and the hardware adds B * sum(x_s) with
+       * B = 0x80 - wt_zp (the B field of the bias record, rkt_fill_biases),
+       * both over every channel the CNA reads,
+       * the padded ones included. A padded channel stored as 0 therefore
+       * weighs B, not 0, and its input byte enters the result. The bias fold
+       * (calculate_weight_sum) cancels that only when the padded input bytes
+       * hold in_zp - 0x80, which is what rkt_ml_subgraph_invoke writes when it
+       * uploads a graph input. A tensor produced by an earlier conv of the
+       * same subgraph is written by the DPU, which leaves the channels past
+       * the real count of its last 16-channel group at 0 (MobileNetV2 op 6,
+       * 56x56x24 -> 144 fed by op 5's NPU output, was off by a constant 49
+       * on every output channel).
+       *
+       * Stored as wt_zp - 0x80 (w_q = wt_zp, what the generic path already
+       * writes for its padded lanes), a padded channel contributes
+       * x_s * (wt_zp - 0x80) + B * x_s = 0 whatever it holds, and the
+       * padded-channel term of calculate_weight_sum goes away with it.
+       */
+      uint8_t pad_w = (uint8_t)(zero_point - 0x80);
+
       for (unsigned oc = 0; oc < oc_n; oc++)
          for (unsigned ic = 0; ic < ic_n; ic++) {
             unsigned n;
@@ -602,10 +626,12 @@ rkt_fill_weights(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
              * fifteen past it. Neither has weights of its own in the tensor,
              * and both stay at the zero point.
              */
-            weights_out[n] = (oc < output_channels_real &&
-                              ic < input_channels_real)
-                                ? weights_in[oc][0][0][ic] - 0x80
-                                : 0;
+            if (oc >= output_channels_real)
+               weights_out[n] = 0;
+            else
+               weights_out[n] = ic < input_channels_real
+                                   ? weights_in[oc][0][0][ic] - 0x80
+                                   : pad_w;
          }
 
       /*
@@ -793,34 +819,9 @@ calculate_weight_sum(const struct pipe_ml_operation *poperation, unsigned oc,
             for (unsigned ic = 0; ic < input_channels; ic++)
                sum += weights[oc][x][y][ic] - weight_zero_point;
       /*
-       * THE PADDED INPUT CHANNELS ARE IN THE HARDWARE'S SUM, so they have to
-       * be in this one.
-       *
-       * Since round 197 the pointwise weight buffer is laid out to
-       * ALIGN(ic, FEATURE_ATOMIC_SIZE) and since round 202 the CNA is told
-       * that count, so the hardware accumulates over the padded channels too.
-       * Their weights are written as biased zero, which is w_q = 0x80, so each
-       * one contributes (0x80 - weight_zero_point) to sum(w_q - wt_zp) and
-       * this loop, which walks the real channels only, missed all of them.
-       *
-       * A[oc] = bias - (in_zp - 0x80) * sw, so a short sw lands as a constant
-       * offset on every pixel of the channel. Round 202 left pw33x64w56 at
-       * slope 0.9997 with the offset collapsed to -35.3..-30.3, standard
-       * deviation 0.85, which is the shape of exactly one missing constant.
-       *
-       * A shape whose ic is already a multiple of the atom pads by nothing and
-       * this term is zero, which is what makes pw64x41w56 and conv2d-cal the
-       * control.
-       *
-       * ROCKET_NO_ICPAD_SUM drops the term.
+       * The padded input channels carry the neutral weight (see
+       * rkt_fill_weights), so they add nothing to the hardware's sum.
        */
-      if (weights_width == 1 && weights_height == 1 &&
-          !getenv("ROCKET_NO_ICPAD_SUM")) {
-         unsigned padded = rkt_pw_ic_padded(input_channels);
-
-         sum += (int32_t)(padded - input_channels) *
-                ((int32_t)0x80 - (int32_t)weight_zero_point);
-      }
    }
    return sum;
 }
